# Line endings.
#
# This pack was committed from Windows without a .gitattributes, so what is
# stored in the repository drifted: 34 JSON files hold CRLF and 3 hold LF, 10
# Lua files hold CRLF and 12 hold LF. The LF ones are the generated and newer
# files -- tools/*.py and any editor under WSL write LF -- and the CRLF ones
# are the original template plus the wiki-built location JSONs.
#
# The cost of that split is silent whole-file churn: a script that reads a
# CRLF file in Python text mode and writes it back produces LF, and every line
# of the file then shows as changed. Adding a "^" to 1723 access rules once
# turned into a 29,000 line diff that way.
#
# text=auto stores LF in the repository and converts on checkout, so a tool
# that writes LF no longer rewrites anything git can see.

* text=auto

# Named explicitly so the setting does not depend on the content heuristic.
*.json  text
*.lua   text
*.py    text
*.md    text

# Never convert, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
